From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1vivy <1vivy@tutanota.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:35:03 -0600
Subject: web: initialize the WASM module inside Web Workers

`initializeWasmModule` and the generated binding assume a page:

- the wasm-bindgen glue is loaded with a <script> element appended to
  `document.head`, which does not exist in a dedicated worker;
- the glue's global is published and read through `window`, which is
  undefined in a worker;
- the init function is invoked through an extension type member named
  `call`, which compiles to `Function.prototype.call(arg)`: the URL is
  passed as `this`, the init function receives no argument, and
  wasm-bindgen falls back to the URL of the current <script>. A worker
  has none.

Load the glue with `importScripts` when there is no `document` (the
path resolves against the worker script URL), publish/read the glue
through `globalThis`, and call the init function with
`callAsFunction(null, url)` so the `_bg.wasm` URL is actually passed.
Page behavior is unchanged: same <script> loading, same URL. The
`package:web` import in generalized_frb_rust_binding/_web.dart goes,
now unused.

No regression test: it needs a compiled wasm-bindgen module running in
a worker, which the package's unit tests do not have. The harness in
the last check below is about 30 lines of Dart plus a page that starts
the worker.

Checks run on 1e4df906 (master after v2.14.0-beta.2; fork branch
web-worker-init @ 9fa0e463), Dart 3.13.7, Chrome 157.0.8103.50
(headless), wasm-pack 0.15.1:
- `dart analyze lib/src/wasm_module lib/src/generalized_frb_rust_binding
  test/wasm_module_web_test.dart` in frb_dart: no issues, at the base
  and with this change.
- `dart test -p chrome test/wasm_module_web_test.dart
  test/consts_web_test.dart test/generalized_uint8list_web_test.dart`:
  3 passed, at the base and with this change.
- A Dart program importing
  package:flutter_rust_bridge/src/wasm_module/_web.dart, compiled with
  `dart compile js -O1` and loaded with `importScripts` in a dedicated
  Web Worker served over HTTP, next to a `no-modules` glue + .wasm pair
  built with `build-web --no-threads`: at the base the module never
  loads (`TypeError: null: type 'JSNull' is not a subtype of type
  'JSObject'` from `web.document.head!`); with this change
  `initializeWasmModule(root: 'probe_wasm')` resolves and the glue's
  `add(2, 3)` returns 5 inside the worker.

Rebase notes: moved from 1e4df906 to v2.13.0, the latest stable
release, without conflicts.

Checked on v2.13.0 with this series, Flutter 3.47.9, Chrome
158.0.8127.36: the p0g web runtime proof (`bash
tool/web_runtime_proof/run.sh frb`, from a clean pub/Cargo fixture
without FRB overrides) built a `build-web --no-threads --release`
module, and generated bindings calling `RustLib.init()` in a dedicated
classic Web Worker (no document, no cross-origin isolation) returned
`"value":"rust:5050","hasDocument":false,"isolated":false,"errors":[]`.
The checks above have not been rerun on v2.13.0.

diff --git a/frb_dart/lib/src/generalized_frb_rust_binding/_web.dart b/frb_dart/lib/src/generalized_frb_rust_binding/_web.dart
index a4f17fe493b2084ab806b40d18a6f7336ee4529e..849226171c33365e66dbb4c3399a02df13668bb5 100644
--- a/frb_dart/lib/src/generalized_frb_rust_binding/_web.dart
+++ b/frb_dart/lib/src/generalized_frb_rust_binding/_web.dart
@@ -5,7 +5,6 @@ import 'dart:js_interop_unsafe';
 
 import 'package:flutter_rust_bridge/src/generalized_uint8list/generalized_uint8list.dart';
 import 'package:flutter_rust_bridge/src/platform_types/_web.dart';
-import 'package:web/web.dart' as web;
 
 /// {@macro flutter_rust_bridge.only_for_generated_code}
 class GeneralizedFrbRustBinding {
@@ -99,7 +98,9 @@ class GeneralizedFrbRustBinding {
 
   /// {@macro flutter_rust_bridge.only_for_generated_code}
   _JSWasmBindgen get _wasmBindgen {
-    final jsObject = web.window.getProperty(_wasmBindgenName.toJS) as JSObject;
+    // globalThis, not window: the binding also runs in Web Workers.
+    final jsObject =
+        globalContext.getProperty(_wasmBindgenName.toJS) as JSObject;
     return _JSWasmBindgen(jsObject);
   }
 }
diff --git a/frb_dart/lib/src/wasm_module/_web.dart b/frb_dart/lib/src/wasm_module/_web.dart
index 82b1f574a69369a83aced74c7ba12437c1b14d96..28d6214f11d4ddd7eb930a7b117c88fe0b7939dd 100644
--- a/frb_dart/lib/src/wasm_module/_web.dart
+++ b/frb_dart/lib/src/wasm_module/_web.dart
@@ -12,18 +12,32 @@ Future<void> initializeWasmModule({
 }) async {
   _ensureCrossOriginIsolated();
 
-  final script = web.HTMLScriptElement()..src = '$root.js';
-  web.document.head!.append(script);
-
-  await script.onLoad.first;
+  // A page loads the wasm-bindgen glue with a <script> tag. A Web Worker
+  // (a Squadron worker, say) has no document, so it uses importScripts,
+  // which resolves [root] against the worker script's URL. Either way the
+  // glue's `let wasm_bindgen` is a global binding; copy it onto globalThis
+  // so it can be read as a property in both.
+  if (globalContext.has('document')) {
+    final script = web.HTMLScriptElement()..src = '$root.js';
+    web.document.head!.append(script);
+    await script.onLoad.first;
+  } else {
+    _importScripts('$root.js'.toJS);
+  }
 
-  jsEval('window.$wasmBindgenName = $wasmBindgenName');
+  jsEval('globalThis.$wasmBindgenName = $wasmBindgenName');
 
-  final jsObject = web.window.getProperty(wasmBindgenName.toJS) as JSObject;
-  final wasmBindgen = _JSWasmBindgen(jsObject);
-  await wasmBindgen('${root}_bg.wasm'.toJS).toDart;
+  // Call the init function itself. `_JSWasmBindgen.call(x)` compiled to
+  // Function.prototype.call(x): no argument reached it, so it fell back to
+  // the URL of the <script> it was loaded from, which a worker does not have.
+  final init = globalContext.getProperty(wasmBindgenName.toJS) as JSFunction;
+  final url = '${root}_bg.wasm'.toJS;
+  await (init.callAsFunction(null, url) as JSPromise).toDart;
 }
 
+@JS('importScripts')
+external void _importScripts(JSString url);
+
 void _ensureCrossOriginIsolated() {
   switch (crossOriginIsolated) {
     case false:
@@ -42,8 +56,3 @@ void _ensureCrossOriginIsolated() {
       return;
   }
 }
-
-extension type _JSWasmBindgen(JSObject _) implements JSObject {
-  @JS()
-  external JSPromise call(JSAny? arg);
-}
